    "tla_configuration_correction": "The first final_only negative used a file chain, whose aliases are conservatively retained by final-identity comparison. It correctly found no violation. Changing that case to a directory alias produces the intended AcceptedReadable violation. Original focused/full reports and corrected run retained; authoritative report substitutes only this corrected case."
  },
  "defect": "Raw retained-name comparison can delete canonical files referenced through stable aliases. Even a separately retained canonical file does not prevent unlink of required partial/sealed aliases. Final canonical ancestors alone miss directories traversed before .. in symlink targets. All occur in stopped standalone single-queue fixtures with genuine accepted WAL roots and no fault injection.",
  "fix": "Inspection-local successful identity and trace caches normalize retained_paths and protect every reference-resolution binding. Apply checks to sealed/pack and partial candidates. Trace errors forbid deletion and uncertain/escaping candidate identities abort inspection. Unlink lexical enumerated names, never substitute resolved targets. Reinspection, stopped-run gate and shared-layout guards remain required.",
  "findings": [
    "Four hosts run 112 baseline and 112 fixed cases across seven alias/reference shapes, 2 KiB/8 MiB payloads and presence/absence of a second canonical accepted root. Baseline loses 56 physical files (235,006,436 bytes) and breaks 32 additional references by deleting route aliases while physical files survive. Fixed has zero losses and every payload read matches.",
    "Both versions reclaim 112 independent orphan packs and 224 orphan/dangling aliases. An unrelated alias target outside raw enumeration survives. All accepted journals are unchanged. Private fixture teardown is separate from intended offline orphan cleanup and intentional unsafe deletion; no catalog GC is claimed.",
    "Twenty-eight local cases per version and two four-case initial reproductions are separate from four-host totals. All private pools and remote execution environments are removed.",
    "The new finite model checks accepted reachability, lexical unlink, refusal on unknown resolution, successful orphan cleanup and conditional termination. Its environment-only negative removes required intermediate bindings; the resulting counterexample identifies the trace assumption."
  ],
