  "limitations": [
    "Complete resolution traces are supplied by the finite model. Python readlink/path traversal, WAL and JSON decoding, closure discovery, report reinspection and actual syscall correspondence are not mechanically refined. This Python change is not claimed as Verus-proved.",
    "External namespace binding stability and actual participant quiescence are caller/environment obligations, not fencing proofs. Algorithm deletion is explicitly allowed in the model and checked; alias preservation is not assumed. Hard-link/bind-mount equivalence is outside the existing namespace contract.",
    "Trace completeness requires truthful readlink success/EINVAL classification. Unknown retained paths disable deletion; unknown/escaping candidate paths abort inspection. The 40-link bound is a Linux path-expansion rejection guard, not a visibility or latency guarantee.",
    "Failed deletion/sync may already have effects. Termination includes explicit refusal and does not establish automatic retries or eventual reclamation under arbitrary faults. No recovery of previously deleted data is provided.",
    "The initial final-file-only negative configuration used a file alias that identity comparison already protects. Original non-triggering runs are retained; the corrected directory-alias case provides the required counterexample. The final report records the targeted replacement explicitly.",
    "All 21 Verus inputs and Rust/native test inputs are identical to prior full checks. Fresh 119 positive Verus checks and Python/wheel tests are separate from reused 105 semantic negatives and 40 native tests.",
    "No new throughput/p99 claim, 100 GB/physical TB run, cold-cache guarantee, full-system proof or claim of no remaining bugs."
  ],
